{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787032754,"nonce":"EnKR0qtF57t31wpUOouo2+gLTWk=","message":"Done in a5786e4 (ADR 0038), with ONE clause deliberately not implemented.\n\nShipped: ComputeGroupKey/SplitLabels in internal/alerts/domain/keys.go over (org, cluster, alertname, namespace-or-∅); group_labels are now oto's axes rather than Alertmanager's; the reconciler's second /api/v2/alerts/groups call is deleted; 00050 rewrites the COMMENTs and argues why there is no backfill.\n\nNOT DONE: alert_groups.receiver and source_group_key are NOT dropped. They are severed from identity and re-commented as provenance. The ticket's escape hatch — that provenance is recoverable from ingest_batches — is false: ingest_batches has no group_id (00006_ingestion.sql:15-49) and alert_groups has no batch_id, so the join does not exist at any retention. Both columns are still READ (the shipped ?receiver= filter and its list ETag basis, the Slack footer, the webhook envelope). Dropping them destroys provenance rather than relocating it, and is an outward API break. Recorded in ADR 0038 and 00050's header.\n\nStorage: the hash is computed in Go and stored in the existing alert_groups.group_key, served by grp_open_idx. The axes stay in group_labels JSONB. Promoting namespace to an indexed column would need an expression index or a NOT NULL DEFAULT '' that destroys the ''≠∅ distinction — the COALESCE trap that 00021 already half-fell into.\n\nSTILL OPEN, and the reason this needs your eye: the axes are UNVALIDATED against real payloads. tools/groupreplay/ runs on synthetic fixtures today and takes -dsn to point at a real ingest_batches (30-day retention, not 14 — 00036_retention_defaults). Run it before trusting the split.\n\nA behavioural regression is recorded, not fixed by the key change itself: two delivery drills inside group_close_delay shared a generation once the nonce left groupLabels. Fixed separately by